---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import MethodologyContent from '../components/MethodologyContent.astro';

const facts = [
  { label: 'Countries visited', value: '154 / 193 UN member states' },
  { label: 'Travel style', value: 'Independent traveller' },
  { label: 'Favourite travel mix', value: 'Beautiful places and difficult places' },
  { label: 'Site focus', value: 'Affordable luxury hotels' },
  { label: 'Mission', value: 'Finding unusually good hotel value worldwide' },
];
---

<PageLayout
  title="About 50 Five-Star Hotels"
  description="About Gary Wilson and the story behind 50 Five-Star Hotels, a personal guide to affordable luxury hotels and five-star hotels without five-star prices."
  image="/images/about/about-gary-wilson-50-five-star-hotels.png"
  maxWidth="max-w-6xl"
>
  <!-- Hero image: full, uncropped, centred -->
  <figure class="mb-12">
    <img
      src="/images/about/about-gary-wilson-50-five-star-hotels.png"
      alt="Illustrated travel infographic about Gary Wilson, his 154-country travel background, and the story behind 50 Five-Star Hotels."
      class="w-full h-auto object-contain mx-auto rounded-2xl border border-[#E2D4BF] shadow-sm bg-[#FFFDF8]"
      style="max-width: 1200px;"
      width="800"
      height="1200"
    />
  </figure>

  <!-- Research prompt promo -->
  <section class="mb-12 rounded-2xl bg-[#F4EADC] border border-[#E2D4BF] px-5 py-12 text-center">
    <p class="text-[#B88A44] text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest mb-4">Hotel Finder</p>
    <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold text-[#1F2428] mb-4">Planning your own trip?</h2>
    <p class="text-[#6F685F] text-lg mb-8 max-w-xl mx-auto">
      Use the Hotel Finder to build a practical shortlist for your own trip. It helps compare hotels by value, five-star reality, location, recent reviews, nearby things to do and honest drawbacks.
    </p>
    <a href="/hotel-finder/" class="inline-flex items-center bg-[#B88A44] text-white font-semibold py-3.5 px-8 rounded-full hover:bg-[#1F2428] transition-colors no-underline text-sm">
      Use the Hotel Finder →
    </a>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <p class="text-[#B88A44] text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest mb-4">The story</p>
    <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl text-[#1F2428] mb-8">About 50 Five-Star Hotels</h1>

    <!-- Credibility fact box -->
    <div class="not-prose bg-[#FFFDF8] border border-[#E2D4BF] rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8 mb-12 shadow-sm">
      <div class="w-10 h-px bg-[#B88A44] mb-5"></div>
      <dl class="space-y-4">
        {facts.map(fact => (
          <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline gap-1 sm:gap-4">
            <dt class="text-[#B88A44] text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest sm:w-44 sm:flex-shrink-0">
              {fact.label}
            </dt>
            <dd class="text-[#1F2428] font-medium">{fact.value}</dd>
          </div>
        ))}
      </dl>
    </div>

    <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none
      prose-headings:font-serif prose-headings:text-[#1F2428]
      prose-h2:text-2xl prose-h2:mt-10 prose-h2:mb-4
      prose-p:text-[#1F2428]/75 prose-p:leading-relaxed
      prose-strong:text-[#1F2428]
      prose-a:text-[#B88A44] prose-a:no-underline hover:prose-a:underline">

      <p>I have visited 154 of the world's 193 United Nations member states.</p>
      <p>
        Over the years I have travelled across every continent, from some of the world's
        most famous destinations to places that rarely appear on tourism lists. I enjoy both
        beautiful places and difficult places: remote mountain regions, little-visited
        countries, historic cities, deserts, tropical islands, and destinations that many
        travellers overlook.
      </p>
      <p>Most of my trips are not luxury trips.</p>
      <p>
        Like many travellers, I usually have a budget. But whenever it has been possible, I
        have enjoyed staying in hotels that offer an unusually high level of comfort,
        character, service, or atmosphere for the price.
      </p>
      <p>What fascinated me was how dramatically hotel value varies around the world.</p>
      <p>
        In some destinations, a standard hotel room can cost more than a luxury suite
        elsewhere. In other places, it is possible to stay in beautiful heritage hotels,
        stylish boutique properties, elegant city hotels, or even genuine five-star resorts
        for far less than many people expect.
      </p>
      <p>Over time I began keeping notes.</p>
      <p>
        Whenever I found a hotel that made me think, &ldquo;I didn't realise I could stay
        somewhere like this for that price,&rdquo; I added it to the list.
      </p>
      <p>
        Eventually the list became large enough that I decided to turn it into this website.
      </p>

      <h2>Why this site exists</h2>
      <p>
        50 Five-Star Hotels is a personal research project dedicated to finding hotels that
        offer an exceptional luxury-to-price ratio.
      </p>
      <p>The goal is not to find the cheapest hotels.</p>
      <p>
        The goal is to find hotels where the experience feels significantly better than the
        price suggests.
      </p>
      <p>
        Some are genuine international five-star hotels. Others are heritage properties,
        boutique hotels, resorts, or locally classified five-star hotels that deliver an
        experience far above what many travellers expect for the cost.
      </p>
      <p>For every hotel, I ask a simple question:</p>
      <p>
        <strong>Would a reasonably experienced traveller be pleasantly surprised by what
        they get for the money?</strong>
      </p>
      <p>If the answer is yes, it deserves consideration. You can read more about how this works in the <a href="/about/#methodology">methodology section</a>.</p>

      <h2>How I travel</h2>
      <p>
        I am particularly interested in unusual destinations, emerging travel destinations,
        historic cities, archaeology and culture, mountains and natural landscapes, food and
        local restaurants, affordable luxury travel, and finding exceptional value.
      </p>
      <p>
        Many of the hotels featured on this site are places I have stayed in, researched
        extensively, or would happily book myself on a future trip. You can browse them all
        by <a href="/destinations">destination</a> or by budget tier, from
        <a href="/under-100">hotels under €100</a> upwards.
      </p>

      <h2>The promise</h2>
      <p>This site is built around a simple idea:</p>
      <p><strong>Five-star hotels without five-star prices.</strong></p>
      <p>
        I believe luxury travel does not have to be reserved for people with unlimited
        budgets. With the right destination, the right timing, and the right hotel,
        remarkable stays can be surprisingly affordable.
      </p>
      <p>
        This website is my attempt to find those opportunities and share them with other
        travellers.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="not-prose mt-12 bg-[#1F2428] rounded-2xl p-8 text-white">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold mb-3">Start exploring</h2>
      <p class="text-white/60 text-sm mb-6">Browse the collection by destination, budget tier or how we choose hotels.</p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a href="/destinations" class="inline-flex items-center bg-[#B88A44] text-white font-semibold py-2.5 px-5 rounded-xl hover:bg-[#A8763A] transition-colors no-underline text-sm">
          Browse by destination
        </a>
        <a href="/under-100" class="inline-flex items-center bg-[#FFFDF8]/10 text-white font-semibold py-2.5 px-5 rounded-xl hover:bg-[#FFFDF8]/20 transition-colors no-underline text-sm">
          Hotels under €100
        </a>
        <a href="#methodology" class="inline-flex items-center bg-[#FFFDF8]/10 text-white font-semibold py-2.5 px-5 rounded-xl hover:bg-[#FFFDF8]/20 transition-colors no-underline text-sm">
          How we choose hotels
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <MethodologyContent />
</PageLayout>
